Implement user story SKY-004-A: Implement Express server routes, validation, and dashboard HTML

## Story Description
Create src/server.ts with all Express route handlers (/health, /search, /cheapest, /) and src/public/index.html dashboard. Export named `app` separately from listen(). Implement param validation, RAPIDAPI_KEY gating, error handling, and Content-Type headers. Depends on SKY-002.

## Acceptance Criteria
- src/server.ts exports a named `app` (Express instance) separately from the listen() call; importing the module does not bind a port or start the server listening
- GET /health returns 200 JSON { status: 'ok', uptime: <positive number> } regardless of RAPIDAPI_KEY presence
- GET / returns 200 text/html with body content matching the contents of src/public/index.html read from the file at runtime; returns 500 JSON { error: string } when src/public/index.html does not exist at runtime; this route is not gated by RAPIDAPI_KEY
- GET /search with valid from/to/date params returns 200 { flights: FlightResult[], count, searchedAt: ISO-8601 } where count equals flights.length; missing or empty-string required param → 400; non-numeric adults → 400; adults defaults to 1 when absent; adults ≤ 0 → 400; invalid date format (not valid YYYY-MM-DD) → 400
- GET /cheapest with valid params returns 200 with the cheapest FlightResult; empty results → 404; missing or empty-string required param → 400; adults defaults to 1 when absent; adults ≤ 0 → 400; invalid date format → 400
- RAPIDAPI_KEY absent → /search and /cheapest return 503 { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' }; /health and / unaffected
- SkyscannerClient error during /search or /cheapest → 500 { error: string } without unhandled promise rejection or server crash; searchedAt is ISO-8601 per-request; the FlightResult shape in responses conforms to the SKY-002 type contract
- All JSON responses from every endpoint include Content-Type: application/json header





