8. Add `GET /cheapest` route: same RAPIDAPI_KEY 503 check and param validation as `/search`; call `SkyscannerClient.search(...)` (or a cheapest-specific method) inside try/catch — if results array is non-empty, return `200` with the cheapest `FlightResult` (lowest `price`); if results are empty, return `404 { error: 'No flights found' }`; on client error return `500 { error: string }`; ensure `Content-Type: application/json` on all responses.

9. At the bottom of `/home/bradleyjerome/projects/skyscanner-app/src/server.ts`, add `if (require.main === module) { const port = process.env.PORT || 3000; app.listen(port, () => console.log(\`Server on \${port}\`)); }` so importing the module does not bind a port.

